# Treat upstream source CSVs as binary — DO NOT normalize line endings.
# The bytes are sha-pinned across manifest.json, web/src/data/csv/index.json,
# and every "this card was in the manifest" citation. Git's default
# CRLF→LF normalization would re-hash the committed bytes (verified
# 2026-05-21 — disk sha f75e2f7d... became git-stored sha d23efd26...
# after the first commit) and break reproducibility for anyone
# downloading from pursueindex.com and shasum-verifying.
data/raw/csv/*.csv binary
web/public/data/csv/*.csv binary

# PDF structure uses CR/LF/CRLF line endings outside its binary streams, and
# xref tables store exact byte offsets — CRLF→LF normalization shifts those
# offsets and corrupts the file (verified: the staged blob differed from the
# working-tree file byte-for-byte after a plain `git add`).
tests/fixtures/*.pdf binary
